estion/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14c7d084-e531-5ec8-b8a4-84313c9c5235" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570920} {:answer/id #uuid "1772de48-db0b-51da-aed0-d21f58c33bb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570923} {:answer/id #uuid "309105f2-241b-59a8-b108-1fbc5ad23672" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570967} {:answer/id #uuid "5046e838-51c7-590f-9148-f9c9e26829ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571015} {:answer/id #uuid "dc8c2bed-cb94-57d8-9276-32a0fd10323b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc8c2bed-cb94-57d8-9276-32a0fd10323b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571230} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fe26995-771e-5e1a-8bdf-3ca759f26bd9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571336}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5fc95051-8b70-5447-aece-290d3854c40e" :question/math-academy-id "q-126481" :question/problem "Consider the matrix \n$D=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $D$ is upper triangular\n\nII. $D$ is lower triangular\n\nIII. ${D}^{T}$ is upper triangular" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false, since $D$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. All the entries above the main diagonal of $D$ are zeros:\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. All the entries below the main diagonal of ${D}^{T}$ are zeros:\n\n$$\n{D}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186571420 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c4d8db6-cf00-5561-9f71-cda33196d5a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571009} {:answer/id #uuid "6ba37546-0b19-5c70-a714-0a34b98342c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571058} {:answer/id #uuid "82a96621-2960-553c-91f5-72e8e13d6f3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571093} {:answer/id #uuid "959c3d53-f156-5e94-9bfd-bec522413d33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571125} {:answer/id #uuid "de7db33e-db49-51d2-a800-9aafb37e46d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571234}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de7db33e-db49-51d2-a800-9aafb37e46d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571234} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b102253-6f2b-5abd-a982-625362c5bac1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571341}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "814b1f0e-0432-56a4-8a3b-10efb7462756" :question/math-academy-id "q-126474" :question/problem "Consider the matrix \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $B$ is upper triangular\n\nII. $B$ is lower triangular\n\nIII. ${B}^{T}+B$ is upper triangular" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false, since $B$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false, since $B$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true, since the result of ${B}^{T}+B$ has all the entries below the main diagonal equal to zero:\n\n$$\n{B}^{T}+B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186571448 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54aa0d5a-e3d8-51a9-8f3b-dff607ae904f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571018} {:answer/id #uuid "5d551e2f-4165-511c-9380-cb5230ba4f24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571039} {:answer/id #uuid "732dcb76-f25b-5bba-ba60-def211538974" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571072} {:answer/id #uuid "bd949b47-98d3-5daf-9d62-c468035cb5ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571184} {:answer/id #uuid "e5620cdc-dc79-59a5-961b-bec9724caa10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571248}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54aa0d5a-e3d8-51a9-8f3b-dff607ae904f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571018} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ee22029-c16e-5aeb-adc2-4fcc4a68c015" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571315}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e901e3e2-6ad0-5a4e-b4c9-fb5111610c41" :question/math-academy-id "q-42114" :question/problem "Consider the matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ is upper triangular\n\nII. $A$ is lower triangular\n\nIII. ${A}^{T}$ is lower triangular" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false, since $A$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false, since $A$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false, since ${A}^{T}$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None\"."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Correct Statements About a Matrix" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050283 :topic/title "Triangular Matrices"}]}]}
